`UnitData.update` loops over unique values from `OrderedDict.fromkeys(data)`. The assignment in question is inside `if val not in self._mapping:`, so whenever execution reaches `self._mapping[val] = next(self._counter)`, the condition `val not in self._mapping` has just been checked and is true. Each test also creates a fresh `UnitData()`, so there is no prior state carried across tests.

